From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:13:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc phone screens from the original Game.exe (0x453800
 and the screen routines)

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) phone is drawn as the original draws it, on the layer GlobalVars[6842] (0x428790):

- Body sliding in with the open counter GlobalVars[6801] (0x453800), the opening animation of the default phone
  (0x45a320, PHONE3), antenna / battery bar (0x44d520), the unread mark, the frame over the screen.
- All screens of the phone modes: home with wallpaper, new mail and incoming call (0x44d8f0, 0x45c150, 0x45a3e0),
  main menu (0x44fb80), mail menu (0x44f5e0), inbox / sent lists with read and answered marks and page numbers
  (0x451f10, 0x451340), received / sent mails and the answer with date, sender, subject, separator, scrolling text
  and scroll arrows (0x452be0, 0x452440, 0x44fe80), the phone trigger mail with its underlined words, blue, the
  chosen one white on blue (0x450980 with 0x444b90 / 0x4453d0), sending / sent notices (0x453640, 0x450530), the
  answer / attachment choice (0x44f4c0, 0x4511a0), address book and call / mail choice (0x453380, 0x453530,
  0x451e50), calling, dialling with the key pad, connecting (0x44dd30, 0x44dfb0, 0x450310, 0x4506f0, 0x450830,
  the moving dotted frames 0x454130 / 0x453e60), settings, wallpapers with thumbnails, call and mail ringtones,
  vibration lists and their set / try panels (0x44e130, 0x44e430, 0x44e860, 0x44eb60, 0x44ef00, 0x44f1e0,
  0x4512d0, 0x451810, 0x451c50, 0x451cc0, 0x451d60, 0x451da0, 0x451dd0, 0x452400), the music player with the
  scrolling title and the play time (0x451870), the mail behind the attachment modes (0x44fb60).
- Panels, choice boxes and title bars (0x45a530, 0x45a620, 0x45bbd0 with the table 0x52e9c0).
- Text as the original lays it out (0x444f70): the phone strings of the mail table, wrapped to the given width,
  skipped / limited lines, line breaks; the line counts of the scroll ranges now use the same layout.
- The phone textures are the ones the scripts load (LoadTexture: 15 MUSIC, 16..20 PHONE.._E, 21 PHONE2, 22 PHONE3,
  23 PWCG, 24 PWCGTHUM); the sg-pc profile lists them as script handled sheets and the phone draws a surface from
  the sheet whose file the script loaded there. The phone design is GlobalVars[6856].

Fixed in the phone logic: the string bases of 10:37:04 are the values stored at the label (not the label numbers).

Not done here: the camera view of mode 12 (the original copies part of the screen into the phone; the frame only),
the attachment overlays (pictures, picture stories, text pages: 0x44f840, 0x44f980, 0x44d120), mouse / touch hit
areas, the keyboard walk over the words of the phone trigger.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, not a real device, original English data): phone opens with the slide, home with
wallpaper, menu with the entry descriptions, mail menu, inbox with the read mark, the prologue mail (date, sender,
subject, separator, text), settings, address book (Daru, PhoneWave, Faris, Mayuri, Lukako) and the call choice.

TYN only.

